{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. Node inputs are presented using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`.\n2. The text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n3. Failures in loading or preparation return `ValidationError::Graph` for inputs queued on an ask builder.\n4. During a `read_node` tool call, the same failures go to the agent as a tool error, and the agent can continue.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Queued inputs use `format`.**\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` sets a custom formatter. It asserts that the chat history contains \"formatted input: source\". It also asserts that the dependency fingerprint is \"source\" and that the node was read exactly once.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` and `agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` assert the presented text and order for several queued inputs. The second also asserts the matching dependency fingerprints.\n- **Use of `format` during `read_node`.** `agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses the `distinct_pages` formatter. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that `read_node` pages contain the formatter-only strings \"ALPHA-CONTENTS\" and \"BETA-CONTENTS\". Dependencies are recorded as the matching fingerprints.\n- **Same retained observation.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the underlying contents after the read. It then asserts that `format()` still returns \"before\" and that `fingerprint()` equals the snapshot's fingerprint. The domain is read once. `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` shows that formatting uses the supplied retained value, even when a re-read could not resolve the node. `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version]` keeps the prepared snapshot after the source changes.\n- **Failure on the ask builder.** `validation_tests.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers a failed read and a failed preparation. These return `ValidationError::Graph(\"read\")` and `ValidationError::Graph(\"render\")`. No agent request is made and no dependency is recorded.\n- **Failure during `read_node`.** `agent/tests.rs#fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes the formatter fail inside `node_content`. It asserts that the agent receives a `read_node` tool result with `is_error` set and the error text. The agent then submits its result, and no dependencies are recorded.\n- **Missing-agent case.** `validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` covers the missing-agent path and the presented inputs.\n\n**Residual note.** The tool-call failure test exercises preparation failure only. A load failure inside a `read_node` call is not tested separately. Both failures reach the tool path through the same `Domain::node_content` error result. The requirement does not give them different handling there, and load failure is tested on the ask-builder path. I do not count this as a gap.\n\nNo acknowledgments or FIXME items apply.",
  "references": "8048d176a8293e95cc92aa446b4513cd36a149d6f42a172bff9e5eae9b604752",
